meta {
  name: Get Session After Undo Approval
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.success: eq true
  res.body.data.slotsRemaining: eq 8
}

docs {
  Mirrors **Get Session After Approve**. Depends on **Undo Approval** having run --
  `slotsRemaining` dropped to `7` when the request was approved, so undoing that approval
  should restore it to the original `8` (see **Sessions / Create Session**'s `slotsTotal`).

  Like its counterpart, this route itself isn't new -- what's actually being tested is that
  `revertApproval`'s transaction really did increment `slots_remaining` back, not just flip
  the request's own status.
}
